@ignamiranda I think that we need the ability to tag nodes as having the same rank even when they don't have a link, for a couple of reasons.
 * Firstly, aside from breaking many existing diagrams, making symmetrical links force the same rank will make it much harder to control the layout of undirected graphs. There are plenty of cases where the data represents an undirected graph but you want to control the presentation anyway. 
 * Secondly, there are scenarios where we may want to place two nodes on the same rank but not draw a link between them and not necessarily have them closer together. While in your model you could use `A ~~~ B` to equalise the rank, doing that still places a "spring" between the nodes in the layout process. Being able to explicitly place two nodes on the same rank without forcing those nodes closer together would be helpful, and the intent would probably be clearer too.

